  ],
  "text": "On Venus, a single day lasts longer than the whole year. Here you spin once a day, and lap the Sun in three hundred sixty five. Venus needs two hundred and forty three of our days to turn around once. But it finishes a full orbit in only two hundred and twenty five. And the slow spin is not even the strange part. Venus turns backwards, so the Sun there rises in the west. Something stopped that spin, then pushed it back the other way. One idea is a huge impact that knocked the whole planet over. The other is its own air, heavy enough to drag the ground to a stop. Venus is not slow by nature. It is a planet that was stopped. Which is why the year there ends before the morning does. Venus is slow. Jupiter is violent. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro"
}
